# Keep the working tree LF on every platform.
#
# This project generates shell scripts and configuration that run inside Linux
# containers regardless of the host, and writes them through
# `fsutil.write_text_lf` for exactly that reason. Letting Git hand a Windows
# checkout CRLF versions of the sources would undo that care at the other end,
# and would fill every diff with line-ending churn the moment the project is
# edited on two machines.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Except what Windows itself runs: cmd.exe misreads labels and blocks in a
# batch file with LF endings (install.cmd, F45).
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary, so Git must not touch them at all.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.kgui binary
